  "solution": {
    "text": "Molisch&rsquo;s test is a chemical test which is used to check for the presence of carbohydrates in a given analyte. It also gives positive test for peptides as they undergo hydrolysis to give saccharides. Carbylamine test is given by primary amine. &nbsp;If a primary amine is present, the isocyanide (carbylamine) is formed which is a foul smelling substance. A purple or magenta coloured adduct gives positive Schiff&#39;s test for aldehydes.<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>List I</td>\t\t\t<td>List II</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Test</td>\t\t\t<td>Functional group /<br />\t\t\tClass of Compound</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(A) Molisch&#39;s Test</td>\t\t\t<td>(I)Carbohydrate</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(B) Molisch&#39;s Test</td>\t\t\t<td>(II)&nbsp;Peptide</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(C) Carbylamine Test</td>\t\t\t<td>(III) Primary amine</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(D) Schiff s Test</td>\t\t\t<td>(IV) Aldehyde</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>",
